    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds a `^^chart` projector that renders a Hazel value as a chart, modeled on the existing\nTable projector. The same labeled-tuple data that feeds tables is naturally chartable, so\nthis gives bar / grouped-bar / line / scatter / pie views of evaluated results.\n\nCharts are described by a new built-in `Chart` ADT. Rendering is done **by d3 itself** (d3\nowns the DOM): the selection/axis/shape code lives in JS, and OCaml recognizes the data and\nhands d3 the container node.\n\n## The `Chart` ADT (`BuiltinsADT.re`)\n\n```\ntype Chart =\n  + BarChart([(label=String, value=Float)])\n  + GroupedBarChart([(name=String, data=[(label=String, value=Float)])])\n  + LineChart([(x=Float, y=Float)])\n  + ScatterChart([(x=Float, y=Float)])\n  + PieChart([(label=String, value=Float)])\n```\n\nBar/Pie share the categorical shape; Line/Scatter share the points shape; GroupedBarChart is\na list of named series. Constructor names are namespaced (`BarChart`, not `Bar`) to avoid the\nflat global constructor namespace (JSON already claims `Float`/`Int`/`String`/`List`/`Bool`).\nRegistered via a single `type_aliases` row.\n\nData must be `Float` in the surface language \u2014 there is **no implicit `Int`\u2192`Float` coercion**\n(use `float_of_int`), matching the ADT's payload types.\n\n## Architecture\n\n- **`ChartCore.re`** \u2014 a pure, D3-free recognizer (`parse_chart : Exp.t => option(chart_spec)`),\n  reusing `TableCore.parse_table` + `HazelJson`'s wrapper stripping. Unit-tested natively. Also\n  exports `is_chart_ctr_ap`, the cheap type-level test that gates auto-display (below).\n- **`ChartProj.re`** \u2014 marshals `chart_spec` to a JS object and drives d3 through **one generic\n  `Attr.create_hook`** (like the existing `ScrollIntoViewHook`). The container `<div>` has no\n  vdom children, so vdom leaves d3's subtree alone across re-renders. Mirrors `TableProj` for\n  `init`/`get`/`placeholder`/`error`.\n- **`prebundle.js`** \u2014 `window.HazelD3.render(el, spec)` dispatches on `spec.kind` using real d3\n  (`d3.axisLeft`/`axisBottom`, `.data().enter()`, `d3.line`, `d3.pie`/`d3.arc`). Series colors come\n  from CSS vars (`--chart-1..8`, an earthy palette in `variables.css`), with native `<title>`\n  tooltips, hover highlight, bar value labels, per-series legends, and pie-legend truncation.\n- Registered in `ProjectorKind` (`^^chart` via lexer + `of_name`), `ProjectorInit`, context menu.\n\nAdding a chart kind is a `chart_spec` variant + a `js_of_spec` branch + a JS render function.\n\n**Grouped series align by label** ([review](https://github.com/hazelgrove/hazel/pull/2350#discussion_r3460638264)):\nthe category axis is the union of every series' labels in first-seen order, and each series looks\nits own values up by label. `series.values : list(option(float))` is positional against that axis,\nwith `None` crossing to JS as `null` so `renderBar` leaves a gap instead of shifting a series'\nremaining bars into another category's slot. Series need not carry the same categories, or the\nsame number of them.\n\n## Auto-display in eval output (`project_charts` setting)\n\nMirrors `project_tables`: a `Chart` value in an evaluated result auto-renders when the **\"Charts\"**\ntoggle is on (Nut menu \u2192 Value Display). No conflict with tables \u2014 tables fire on bare list\nliterals, charts on `Chart`-constructor applications. Off by default (opt-in), like Tables.\n\nThe gate is the constructor's **type**, not its name\n([review](https://github.com/hazelgrove/hazel/pull/2350#discussion_r3431328434)):\n`is_chart_ctr_ap` peels arrows off the type statics puts on the constructor and compares the\nresult against `BuiltinsADT.Chart.t`. Every variant is covered without enumerating names, and a\nuser ADT that shadows a Chart constructor name is not projected as a chart.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `test/Test_ChartCore.re` (17 cases): all kinds incl. grouped, empty/ragged/non-finite data,\n  Int-value rejection, a positional-tuple case verifying the ADT registration drives\n  auto-labeling, grouped series with differing and short label lists, and the auto-display gate\n  (accepts all five constructors; rejects a shadowed constructor name and unelaborated syntax).\n- `make dev` builds clean; `make test-quick` passes (3326 tests).\n- Manually verified rendering for every kind in the browser (manual `^^chart` and auto-display).\n  The label-union grouped rendering wants one more browser pass.\n\n## Notes / trade-offs\n\n- ~~Grouped/multi-series bars are supported by the recognizer but not reachable through the\n  single-value-column ADT\u2026 open question whether to add a dedicated grouped-bar constructor.~~\n  **Resolved:** added the `GroupedBarChart` constructor (typed, explicit), rendered with\n  per-series colors + a legend.\n- A multi-numeric-column inner `data` table is unreachable from a well-typed program (the ADT\n  types the payload as a single `(label, value)` list), so `parse_grouped` reads the first\n  numeric column and says so in a comment rather than guarding it. The multi-column path in\n  `parse_categorical` is deliberate \u2014 that's how one wide-format `BarChart` becomes grouped.\n- d3 owning the DOM means per-kind drawing lives in JS \u2014 outside OCaml's type checker and unit\n  tests. In exchange it's less code overall and each kind is cheap to add; the recognizer\n  (`ChartCore`) stays pure OCaml and is what the tests cover.\n- Adds `d3-scale`/`d3-array`/`d3-selection`/`d3-axis`/`d3-shape` (`bundled.js` ~1.1 MB).\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
